From 7e1972372ac031a3e7eaf9c8b8937213b081f11c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan B <bbigari@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:25:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Track machine-shaped queries as AI Visibility prompts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the loop between the two features: a query assistants are already
issuing is the best evidence of what is worth monitoring, so selecting rows
sends them straight to the project's tracker instead of being retyped.

Only formatting is stripped from the query — quotes, markdown, operators —
because the wording is the thing worth tracking.

Prompts merge rather than replace: the save path clones the existing
configuration and applies a patch, so adding from here cannot disturb
prompts already on the tracker, and duplicates come back as skipped. The
toast reports what actually landed rather than echoing the count selected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JTBKYzux1gqV8tvd3Q9XBN
